#################################################################
#    Documentation annotations
#################################################################

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/capability#>
    rdfs:comment "A vocabulary for capabilities and capability domains in a digital-twin model, with example capabilities for sharing data and managing data products. The current vocabulary does not define the relationships assigning capabilities to domains."@en ;
    <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/capability#Capability>
    rdfs:comment "An ability represented in the digital-twin capability model, such as the ability to share data or manage data products."@en .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/capability#CapabilityDomain>
    rdfs:label "Capability Domain"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "A subject area used to organize capabilities in a capability model. This vocabulary does not yet declare the relationship assigning capabilities to a domain."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/capability#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/capability#Data_Sharing_and_Marketplace>
    rdfs:label "Data sharing and marketplace"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The example capability covering the sharing of data and its provision through a marketplace."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/capability#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/capability#Designing_and_Managing_Data_Products>
    rdfs:label "Designing and managing data products"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The example sub-capability covering the design and management of data products."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/capability#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/capability#SubCapability>
    rdfs:comment "A more specific capability represented at a subordinate level of a capability model. The current vocabulary declares it independently and does not assert a subclass relationship to Capability."@en .
